scc_sizes: [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]
hamiltonian_paths: 1
edges: score>c3, score>c4, score>c5, score>c6, H>score, c4>c3, c5>c3, c3>c6, H>c3, c4>c5, c4>c6, H>c4, c5>c6, H>c5, H>c6
selected explanation strengths:
  U(c3|score)=1.0000
  U(c5|score)=0.6620
  U(H|c5)=0.6886
  U(H|c6)=0.5121
  U(c6|H)=0.8488

=== Interpretation ===
1. Trace formulas are exact through length 5 because non-simple closed walks need two cycles.
2. Length 6 is the first correction: double triangles and intersecting triangle pairs.
3. c6 is still fast, but it is the first trace invariant needing cycle-placement data p33_meet.
4. At n=6, the low cycle vector (c3,c4,c5,c6) determines H; score+c5+c6 still mixes.
5. The next speed frontier is to test whether corrected trace vectors keep compressing H at n>=7.
